Stopped by around 3 PM when the restaurant didn't seem very busy, but unfortunately the experience didn't match the pace. It took about 40 minutes for the food to arrive, which felt longer than expected given how quiet it was.

We ordered the fattoush salad, which was surprisingly small for a $20 dish, and the eggplant, which was undercooked and not something I'd recommend. The hummus and falafel were decent, but it was noticeable that they had been sitting out for a while--the edges of the hummus were already changing color.

On a more positive note, the chicken schnitzel was a generous portion and tasted pretty good overall, though the side salad was soggy and took away from the dish a bit.

Overall, a mixed experience with some highlights, but enough issues that I wouldn't rush back.

